; Crash Capsule optical transport envelope (normative for the MVP monochrome mode).
;
; Layering, outermost last:
;
;   capsule (deterministic CBOR)
;     -> zstd
;     -> COSE authenticated/encrypted payload
;     -> source symbols of fixed size
;     -> outer Reed-Solomon repair symbols
;     -> frame = header + symbol, drawn as a QR code with its own inner ECC
;
; Rules the decoder depends on:
;
;   1. The sender loops source and repair symbols indefinitely. There is no final
;      frame, and the receiver MUST NOT require catching any particular frame.
;   2. FEC is not integrity. A stream that reassembles is still rejected unless the
;      COSE verification over the reassembled payload succeeds.
;   3. A frame whose header does not match the session the receiver is assembling is
;      discarded, not merged.
;   4. Receivers MUST reject blurred, transition-contaminated, excessively skewed or
;      otherwise low-quality frames rather than feeding uncertain bits into the FEC
;      decoder.
;   5. A dynamic payload MUST NOT be used to open a URL. The static bootstrap QR is the
;      only place a URL may appear, and it is a fixed, verified endpoint.

visual-frame = {
  0 => 1,               ; envelope version
  1 => bstr .size 8,    ; session_id, random per transfer
  2 => uint,            ; total number of source symbols
  3 => uint,            ; symbol size in bytes
  4 => uint,            ; symbol index; >= total means a repair symbol
  5 => bstr,            ; symbol payload
  6 => uint,            ; payload_len, total compressed+encrypted length
  7 => fec-scheme,
  8 => bstr .size 4,    ; truncated SHA-256 of the reassembled payload, a fast pre-check
  ? 9 => uint,          ; profile id, so a receiver can size buffers before assembly
  * uint => any
}

fec-scheme = 0 / 1      ; 0 none (single-symbol payloads), 1 Reed-Solomon over GF(256)

; The static bootstrap QR is not a frame: it is a short ASCII URL to a fixed decoder
; endpoint, optionally with a panic-minimal capsule in the fragment. It never carries
; P2 or higher material.
